{"context": "published", "host": "www.josephsmithpapers.org", "showHeader": true, "footerStyle": "mini", "statusCode": 200, "uri": "letter-from-oliver-cowdery-6-november-1829", "page": "1", "is404": false, "gallery": [{"image": "/25/25_ms155_2_01_lb1_006_thumb.jpg", "page": "1", "label": "6", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-from-oliver-cowdery-6-november-1829/1"}, {"image": "/25/25_ms155_2_01_lb1_007_thumb.jpg", "page": "2", "label": "7", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-from-oliver-cowdery-6-november-1829/2"}, {"image": "/25/25_ms155_2_01_lb1_008_thumb.jpg", "page": "3", "label": "8", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-from-oliver-cowdery-6-november-1829/3"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "letter-from-oliver-cowdery-6-november-1829", "series": "JSPPD", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPD1", "documentSeriesTitle": "Letter from Oliver Cowdery, 6 November 1829", "editorialPageNumber": "6", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/26049/26049-0001.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent wasptag\">Letter 4<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12647604193357905487\"><a href=\"#12647604193357905487\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans1\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">This scribal notation, in the handwriting of <a href=\"/person/frederick-granger-williams\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Frederick G. Williams</a>, indicates that this was the fourth letter copied into <a href=\"/paper-summary/letterbook-1\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letterbook-1\" poptitle=\"Letterbook 1\">JS Letterbook 1</a>.</p><hr></div></div></aside> <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4841804410970059627\"><a href=\"#4841804410970059627\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc15\" place=\"plc15\" title=\"Manchester Township, New York\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">Manchester</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Manchester Township, New York\"><p>Settled 1793. Formed as Burt Township when divided from Farmington Township, 31 Mar. 1821. Name changed to Manchester, 16 Apr. 1822. Included village of Manchester. Population in 1825 about 2,700. Population in 1830 about 2,800. JS reported first vision of...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/manchester-township-new-york\">More Info</a></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7666646086971972353\"><a href=\"#7666646086971972353\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans1\"><span id=\"documenttrans1\">1</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">At the time he wrote this letter, <a href=\"/person/oliver-cowdery\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Cowdery</a> was likely at the <a href=\"/person/hyrum-smith\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Hyrum Smith</a> residence in <a href=\"/place/palmyra-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Palmyra</a>. If this is the case, the letter was written in Palmyra, not in <a href=\"/place/manchester-township-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Manchester</a>.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">November the 6</span><span class=\"josephswriting\">th.</span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> 1829</span></div><div class=\"center wasptag\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">Brother Joseph Smith J</span><span class=\"underscore\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">r</span></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">.</span></div><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><div class=\" indent left wasptag\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">I received your </span><a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" class=\"reference\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" poptitle=\"Letter to Oliver\nCowdery, 22 October 1829\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">leter</span></a><span class=\"josephswriting\"> yesterday bearing date </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">Oct. 22d</span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">I had long time expectted to hear from you</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13367374077170209925\"><a href=\"#13367374077170209925\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans2\"><span id=\"documenttrans2\">2</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">More than a month had passed since JS’s departure from <a href=\"/place/manchester-township-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Manchester</a>. (See <a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" poptitle=\"Letter to Oliver\nCowdery, 22 October 1829\">Letter to Oliver Cowdery, 22 Oct. 1829</a>.)</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> and had often </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">enquired at the post office for a letter and of course it was </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">gladly received by us all</span><span class=\"josephswriting\">.</span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> we rejoice to hear that you are </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">well and we </span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> also rejoice to hear that you have </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">a prospect of obtaining Some mony</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"3691895404349548644\"><a href=\"#3691895404349548644\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans3\"><span id=\"documenttrans3\">3</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/oliver-cowdery\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Cowdery</a> referred here to JS’s report of <a href=\"/person/josiah-stowell-sr\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Josiah Stowell</a>’s willingness to invest “five or six hundred dollars” in the publication of the <a href=\"/paper-summary/book-of-mormon-1830\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/book-of-mormon-1830\" poptitle=\"Book of Mormon, 1830\">Book of Mormon</a>. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" poptitle=\"Letter to Oliver\nCowdery, 22 October 1829\">Letter to Oliver Cowdery, 22 Oct. 1829</a>.)</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> and we further rejo</span><span class=\"josephswriting\">i</span><span class=\"josephswriting\">ce </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">that you are at rest from your percecutors and we rejoice </span> [p. 6]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent wasptag\">&lt;​Let[ter] 4​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"19842584560221264\"><a href=\"#19842584560221264\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans1\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">This scribal notation, in the handwriting of <a href=\"/person/frederick-granger-williams\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Frederick G. Williams</a>, indicates that this was the fourth letter copied into <a href=\"/paper-summary/letterbook-1\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letterbook-1\" poptitle=\"Letterbook 1\">JS Letterbook 1</a>.</p><hr></div></div></aside> &lt;​<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6489601839150742535\"><a href=\"#6489601839150742535\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc15\" place=\"plc15\" title=\"Manchester Township, New York\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">Manchester</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Manchester Township, New York\"><p>Settled 1793. Formed as Burt Township when divided from Farmington Township, 31 Mar. 1821. Name changed to Manchester, 16 Apr. 1822. Included village of Manchester. Population in 1825 about 2,700. Population in 1830 about 2,800. JS reported first vision of...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/manchester-township-new-york\">More Info</a></div></div></aside>​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4772857152717961809\"><a href=\"#4772857152717961809\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans1\"><span id=\"documenttrans1\">1</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">At the time he wrote this letter, <a href=\"/person/oliver-cowdery\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Cowdery</a> was likely at the <a href=\"/person/hyrum-smith\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Hyrum Smith</a> residence in <a href=\"/place/palmyra-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Palmyra</a>. If this is the case, the letter was written in Palmyra, not in <a href=\"/place/manchester-township-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Manchester</a>.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">November the 6</span><span class=\"superscript\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">th.</span></span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> 1829</span></div><div class=\"center wasptag\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">Brother Joseph Smith J</span><span class=\"superscript\"><span class=\"underscore\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">r</span></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">.</span></span></div><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><div class=\" indent left wasptag\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">I received your </span><a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" class=\"reference\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" poptitle=\"Letter to Oliver\nCowdery, 22 October 1829\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">leter</span></a><span class=\"josephswriting\"> yesterday bearing date </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">Oct. 22d</span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">I had long time expectted to hear from you</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"15012132050324601725\"><a href=\"#15012132050324601725\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans2\"><span id=\"documenttrans2\">2</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">More than a month had passed since JS’s departure from <a href=\"/place/manchester-township-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Manchester</a>. (See <a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" poptitle=\"Letter to Oliver\nCowdery, 22 October 1829\">Letter to Oliver Cowdery, 22 Oct. 1829</a>.)</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> and had often </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">enquired at the post office for a letter and of course it was </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">gladly received by us all</span>[<span class=\"josephswriting\">.</span>]<span class=\"josephswriting\"> we rejoice to hear that you are </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">well and we </span><span class=\"deleted\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">expect</span></span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> also rejoice to hear that you have </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">a prospect of obtaining Some mony</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6394629409096442241\"><a href=\"#6394629409096442241\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans3\"><span id=\"documenttrans3\">3</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/oliver-cowdery\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Cowdery</a> referred here to JS’s report of <a href=\"/person/josiah-stowell-sr\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Josiah Stowell</a>’s willingness to invest “five or six hundred dollars” in the publication of the <a href=\"/paper-summary/book-of-mormon-1830\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/book-of-mormon-1830\" poptitle=\"Book of Mormon, 1830\">Book of Mormon</a>. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" poptitle=\"Letter to Oliver\nCowdery, 22 October 1829\">Letter to Oliver Cowdery, 22 Oct. 1829</a>.)</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> and we further rejo</span>[<span class=\"josephswriting\">i</span>]<span class=\"josephswriting\">ce </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">that you are at rest from your percecutors and we rejoice </span> [p. 6]</div></body></html>", "historicalIntro": {"text": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9917730517665865338\"><a href=\"#9917730517665865338\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per47\" person=\"per47\" title=\"Oliver Cowdery\">Oliver Cowdery</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Cowdery, Oliver\"><p>3 Oct. 1806–3 Mar. 1850. Clerk, teacher, justice of the peace, lawyer, newspaper editor. Born at Wells, Rutland Co., Vermont. Son of William Cowdery and Rebecca Fuller. Raised Congregationalist. Moved to western New York and clerked at a store, ca. 1825–1828...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/oliver-cowdery\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside> composed this letter in response to JS’s <a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" class=\"reference\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" poptitle=\"Letter to Oliver\nCowdery, 22 October 1829\">letter</a> two weeks earlier.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11543736070433822240\"><a href=\"#11543736070433822240\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"intro1\"><span id=\"documentintro1\">1</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" poptitle=\"Letter to Oliver\nCowdery, 22 October 1829\">Letter to Oliver Cowdery, 22 Oct. 1829</a>.</p><hr></div></div></aside> By this time Cowdery had been involved with the printing of the <a href=\"/paper-summary/book-of-mormon-1830\" class=\"reference\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/book-of-mormon-1830\" poptitle=\"Book of Mormon, 1830\">Book of Mormon</a> for several weeks, and here he provided JS with a brief update of that work. He also informed JS of the estimated date of completion and explained that illness had delayed the work. In the postscript, Cowdery noted his progress copying the original Book of Mormon manuscript. Pages of the resulting “printer’s manuscript” were then delivered to the printer, <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1668855105712908589\"><a href=\"#1668855105712908589\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per72\" person=\"per72\" title=\"Egbert Bratt Grandin\">E. B. Grandin</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Grandin, Egbert Bratt\"><p>30 Mar. 1806–16 Apr. 1845. Printer, newspaper editor and publisher, butcher, shipper, tanner. Born in Freehold, Monmouth Co., New Jersey. Son of William Grandin and Amy Lewis. Moved to Williamson, Ontario Co., New York, by 1810; to Pultneyville, Ontario Co...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/egbert-bratt-grandin\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside>, ensuring that if the copy were damaged, either through mischief or carelessness, the original would still be preserved.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13959067544830925676\"><a href=\"#13959067544830925676\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"intro2\"><span id=\"documentintro2\">2</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Lucy Mack Smith, History, 1844–1845, <a href=\"/paper-summary/lucy-mack-smith-history-1844-1845/105\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/lucy-mack-smith-history-1844-1845\" poptitle=\"Book 9\">bk. 9</a>, [2]; John H. Gilbert, Memorandum, 8 Sept. 1892, photocopy, CHL.</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\">Gilbert, John H. Memorandum, 8 Sept. 1892. Photocopy. CHL. <a href=\"https://catalog.churchofjesuschrist.org/assets?id=162efea4-cb3f-459f-937f-949b3995e572&amp;crate=0&amp;index=0\" class=\"externalLink\">MS 9223</a>.</p></div></div></div></aside> The sentiments and language of Cowdery’s expressions of faith in the letter reveal his familiarity with passages from the manuscript.</div></body></html>", "footnotes": [{"id": "11543736070433822240", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" poptitle=\"Letter to Oliver\nCowdery, 22 October 1829\">Letter to Oliver Cowdery, 22 Oct. 1829</a>.</p></body></html>", "number": 1, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "13959067544830925676", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">Lucy Mack Smith, History, 1844–1845, <a href=\"/paper-summary/lucy-mack-smith-history-1844-1845/105\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/lucy-mack-smith-history-1844-1845\" poptitle=\"Book 9\">bk. 9</a>, [2]; John H. Gilbert, Memorandum, 8 Sept. 1892, photocopy, CHL.</p></body></html>", "number": 2, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": "<p id=\"source-note1\">Gilbert, John H. Memorandum, 8 Sept. 1892. Photocopy. CHL. <a href=\"https://catalog.churchofjesuschrist.org/assets?id=162efea4-cb3f-459f-937f-949b3995e572&amp;crate=0&amp;index=0\" class=\"externalLink\">MS 9223</a>.</p>"}]}, "sourceNotes": {"text": "<html><head></head><body><span class=\"source-note-summary\"> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14603731499521725430\"><a href=\"#14603731499521725430\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per47\" person=\"per47\" title=\"Oliver Cowdery\">Oliver Cowdery</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Cowdery, Oliver\"><p>3 Oct. 1806–3 Mar. 1850. Clerk, teacher, justice of the peace, lawyer, newspaper editor. Born at Wells, Rutland Co., Vermont. Son of William Cowdery and Rebecca Fuller. Raised Congregationalist. Moved to western New York and clerked at a store, ca. 1825–1828...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/oliver-cowdery\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside>, Letter, <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17784232336300187937\"><a href=\"#17784232336300187937\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc15\" place=\"plc15\" title=\"Manchester Township, New York\">Manchester Township</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Manchester Township, New York\"><p>Settled 1793. Formed as Burt Township when divided from Farmington Township, 31 Mar. 1821. Name changed to Manchester, 16 Apr. 1822. Included village of Manchester. Population in 1825 about 2,700. Population in 1830 about 2,800. JS reported first vision of...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/manchester-township-new-york\">More Info</a></div></div></aside>, Ontario Co., NY, to JS, [<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"18014693824909769511\"><a href=\"#18014693824909769511\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc20\" place=\"plc20\" title=\"Harmony Township, Pennsylvania\">Harmony Township</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Harmony Township, Pennsylvania\"><p>Located in northeastern Pennsylvania. Area settled, by 1787. Organized 1809. Population in 1830 about 340. Population in 1840 about 520. Contained Harmony village (no longer in existence). Josiah Stowell hired JS to help look for treasure in area, Oct. 1825...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/harmony-township-pennsylvania\">More Info</a></div></div></aside>, Susquehanna Co., PA], 6 Nov. 1829. Featured version copied [between ca. 27 Nov. 1832 and ca. Jan. 1833] in <a href=\"/paper-summary/letterbook-1/18\" class=\"reference\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/letterbook-1\" poptitle=\"Letter from Oliver Cowdery • 6 November\n 1829\">JS Letterbook 1, pp. 6–8</a>; handwriting of JS; JS Collection, CHL. For more complete source information, see the source note for <a href=\"/paper-summary/letterbook-1\" class=\"reference\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letterbook-1\" poptitle=\"Letterbook 1\">JS Letterbook 1</a>.</div></span></body></html>", "footnotes": []}, "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [{"versionTitle": "Letter from Oliver Cowdery, 6 November 1829", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/letter-from-oliver-cowdery-6-november-1829/1", "versionFeatured": "true"}, {"versionTitle": "Letterbook 1", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/letterbook-1/18", "versionFeatured": ""}], "images": {"smallImageUrl": "/25/25_ms155_2_01_lb1_006_thumb.jpg", "mediumImageUrl": "/25/25_ms155_2_01_lb1_006_med.jpg", "largeImageUrl": "/25/25_ms155_2_01_lb1_006.jpg", "downloadImageUrl": "/25/25_ms155_2_01_lb1_006_download.jpg"}, "imageCredit": "", "facsimile": "", "dzUrlXml": "/25/25_ms155_2_01_lb1_006.xml", "classification": "Documents", "publishedStatus": "FinalContent", "accessionNumber": "25", "requestedPageNumber": "1", "numberOfPages": "3", "editorialTitle": "Letter from Oliver Cowdery, 6 November 1829", "cleanEditorialTitle": "Letter from Oliver Cowdery, 6 November 1829", "date": "November 6, 1829", "handwriting": "Handwriting of JS", "footnotes": [{"id": "19842584560221264", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">This scribal notation, in the handwriting of <a href=\"/person/frederick-granger-williams\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Frederick G. Williams</a>, indicates that this was the fourth letter copied into <a href=\"/paper-summary/letterbook-1\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letterbook-1\" poptitle=\"Letterbook 1\">JS Letterbook 1</a>.</p></body></html>", "number": null, "type": "scribal", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "4772857152717961809", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">At the time he wrote this letter, <a href=\"/person/oliver-cowdery\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Cowdery</a> was likely at the <a href=\"/person/hyrum-smith\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Hyrum Smith</a> residence in <a href=\"/place/palmyra-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Palmyra</a>. If this is the case, the letter was written in Palmyra, not in <a href=\"/place/manchester-township-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Manchester</a>.</p></body></html>", "number": 1, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "15012132050324601725", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">More than a month had passed since JS’s departure from <a href=\"/place/manchester-township-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Manchester</a>. (See <a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" poptitle=\"Letter to Oliver\nCowdery, 22 October 1829\">Letter to Oliver Cowdery, 22 Oct. 1829</a>.)</p></body></html>", "number": 2, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "6394629409096442241", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/oliver-cowdery\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Cowdery</a> referred here to JS’s report of <a href=\"/person/josiah-stowell-sr\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Josiah Stowell</a>’s willingness to invest “five or six hundred dollars” in the publication of the <a href=\"/paper-summary/book-of-mormon-1830\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/book-of-mormon-1830\" poptitle=\"Book of Mormon, 1830\">Book of Mormon</a>. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-to-oliver-cowdery-22-october-1829\" poptitle=\"Letter to Oliver\nCowdery, 22 October 1829\">Letter to Oliver Cowdery, 22 Oct. 1829</a>.)</p></body></html>", "number": 3, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}], "meta": {"/paper-summary-PageTitle": "Letter from Oliver Cowdery, 6 November 1829, Page 6", "/paper-summary-MetaTitle": "Letter from Oliver Cowdery, 6 November 1829, Page 6", "/paper-summary-MetaDescription": "Letter 4This scribal notation, in the handwriting of Frederick G. Williams, indicates that this was ...", "/paper-summary-MetaUrl": "/paper-summary/letter-from-oliver-cowdery-6-november-1829/1", "/paper-summary-MetaImage": "/bc-jsp/content/jsp/images/25/25_ms155_2_01_lb1_006_thumb.jpg"}, "scribes": [{"id": "per63", "name": "Frederick G. Williams"}, {"id": "per46", "name": "Joseph Smith Jr."}], "printVolumeLocation": "<a href=\"http://www.josephsmithpapers.org/publishedVolumes/documents-volume-1-july-1828-june-1831\" class=\"externalLink\" xmlns:srchdoc=\"https://ldsc.xmlref.com/local/ldschurch/searchDocuments\" xmlns:lds=\"https://ldsc.xmlref.com/local/ldschurch\"><span class=\"title\">JSP,</span> D1:98–101</a>"}, "legal": {}, "disableVerticalScroll": true, "documentURI": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/26049/26049-0001.xml", "searchOptions": [{"name": "| This Document", "value": "document"}, {"name": "| Full Site", "value": "site"}]}